# Who must review a change before it can reach `main`.
#
# The pattern `*` covers every file in the repository, so every pull request
# requires a review from the owner below.
#
# This exists because of a specific gap: branch protection can require "1
# approval", and with two collaborators that approval can come from each other.
# Requiring a review from a CODEOWNER instead means the approval has to come
# from the person named here, whoever else has already looked at it.
#
# Collaborators push their own branches and open pull requests; nothing lands
# on `main` until it is approved here.

* @JiviteshKumar
